invariant: INV-4
file: handshake_flight.c
catches: test/lint-invariants.sh
reason: hsf_begin draws the ClientHello random twice. The second call is a
  fourth site in a function that holds three admitted ones, so
  inv-4-randomness-files passes it, and nobody audited what it draws or
  why. inv-4-randomness-calls refuses a fourth call in hsf_begin, and it
  counts the ML-KEM seed draw under #ifdef CH_KEX_HYBRID as the third.
  This call passed while build_client_hello_ek's header was split across
  #if and #else, because Semgrep skipped the whole file.

--- old
    ch_rand_bytes(h->random, sizeof h->random);
#ifdef CH_KEX_HYBRID
--- new
    ch_rand_bytes(h->random, sizeof h->random);
    ch_rand_bytes(h->random, sizeof h->random);
#ifdef CH_KEX_HYBRID
